---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Topbar from '../components/Topbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Sound Dip — A Directory of Sound Baths"
  description="Who runs Sound Dip, why it exists, and how we choose the practitioners and sessions we list. Vetted, not aggregated."
  canonical="/about"
>
  <main>
    <Topbar />
    <article class="static-page">
      <header class="static-head">
        <div class="static-num">§</div>
        <h1>About <em>Sound Dip.</em></h1>
      </header>

      <section class="prose">
        <h2>What this is</h2>
        <p>Sound Dip is a small directory of sound bath sessions and practitioners across the United States. It exists for one reason: finding a sound bath in most cities is far harder than it should be. The sessions are out there — in yoga studios, borrowed rooms, parks, and a few purpose-built spaces — but they are scattered across Eventbrite pages, Instagram accounts, and studio schedules that never link to each other.</p>
        <p>We built the index that was missing. Instead of a map with a thousand undifferentiated pins, we publish a shorter list of practitioners we can actually describe, organized by city, with the details that matter before you book: format, instruments, price, group size, and what the room is actually like.</p>

        <h2 id="philosophy">Editorial philosophy</h2>
        <p>Our standard is <em>vetted, not aggregated</em>. We would rather list five practitioners we can stand behind than fifty we cannot describe. Every listing we publish gets an original write-up written by a person, not scraped from a business listing or generated in bulk. If we cannot say something specific and true about a session, we leave it out.</p>
        <p>That means the directory is smaller than it could be, and we are comfortable with that. A shorter list with real descriptions beats a longer list of names and outbound links.</p>

        <h2 id="curation">How we choose listings</h2>
        <p>We find practitioners the way a careful newcomer would: through their own websites, published schedules, and event platforms, then we confirm what we can against public information. We note what each practitioner actually offers, where the sessions happen, and how to book.</p>
        <p>Listings carry an honest status. Sessions we have reviewed and verified are marked <em>Verified online</em>. We do not claim to have attended every session in person, and we will not label something "vetted in person" unless it actually was. If we cannot confirm a practitioner, we do not publish them.</p>
        <p>Practitioners can also add or correct their own listings, and they go through a short verification step before they appear.</p>

        <h2 id="who">Who runs this</h2>
        <div class="author">
          <img
            src="/img/team/chester-beard.webp"
            width="533"
            height="800"
            alt="Chester Beard, editor of Sound Dip"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <div>
            <div class="author-name">Chester Beard</div>
            <div class="author-role">Editor · Sound Dip · Puget Sound</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>I'm Chester Beard. I live in the Puget Sound region and I've spent most of my career as a technical writer and brand storyteller — which is a long way of saying I get paid to explain complicated things clearly.</p>
        <p>I grew up in an Episcopal household. The tradition was there from the start. So were the questions. I began looking into other spiritual paths early, and I never really stopped. Kierkegaard was an early influence: faith is not something you inherit — you have to live it yourself or it isn't yours. That idea stuck with me. Then came Hesse's <em>Siddhartha</em>, Sartre's existentialism, a meditation cushion, a yoga mat, and eventually my first sound bath.</p>
        <p>I didn't expect much. I left surprised.</p>
        <p>Here's the problem I kept running into afterward. Finding the next one was awful. Directory sites listing events that happened two years ago. Aggregators scraping each other. Descriptions that clearly came from someone who has never sat through a session. I'd spend an evening scrolling and end up with nothing I trusted.</p>
        <p>So I built this site.</p>
        <p>The rule here is the one those very different writers taught me: don't take it on someone else's word. Try it and see. Every listing is verified by a human — me. Venue confirmed, schedule checked, booking link tested. If I haven't confirmed it, it doesn't go up. If a session doesn't work the way others describe it, I say so.</p>
        <p><strong>Vetted, not aggregated. That's the whole pitch.</strong></p>
        <p>When I'm not vetting listings, I do conservation work with groups like the Sierra Club and The Nature Conservancy, and I write about the Salish Sea region.</p>

        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions, corrections, or a session you think belongs here? Email me at <a href="mailto:hello@sounddip.com">hello@sounddip.com</a>. I read everything and reply when I can.</p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <JsonLd data={{
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Chester Beard",
      "jobTitle": "Editor",
      "image": "https://sounddip.com/img/team/chester-beard.webp",
      "email": "mailto:hello@sounddip.com",
      "homeLocation": { "@type": "Place", "name": "Puget Sound region, Washington" },
      "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Sound Dip", "url": "https://sounddip.com/" }
    }} />

    <JsonLd data={{
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Sound Dip",
      "url": "https://sounddip.com/",
      "email": "hello@sounddip.com",
      "slogan": "Vetted, not aggregated.",
      "founder": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Chester Beard" }
    }} />
    <Footer />
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .static-page {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 140px 6vw 80px;
  }
  .static-head {
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }
  .static-num {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 48px;
    color: var(--clay);
    line-height: 0.8;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .static-head h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 72px);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -2px;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144;
  }
  .static-head h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--clay); }

  .prose {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 72;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 56px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144;
  }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 24px; color: var(--ink-mid); }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--clay);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .prose a:hover { color: var(--clay-d); }

  /* Named editor — the E-E-A-T fix. A real person, a real photo, on the page. */
  .author {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 28px;
    margin: 8px 0 36px;
  }
  .author img {
    width: 128px;
    height: 192px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 20%;
    border-radius: 4px;
    filter: saturate(0.92);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .author-name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .author-role {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .static-page { padding: 100px 6vw 60px; }
    .prose { font-size: 17px; }
    .author { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 20px; }
  }
</style>
